--- !u!114 &1927138055
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1927138054}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: eac827fa24e617e478912ae0761ce9f5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  buttonEdit: 0
  readme: "Steps:\n\n1). Go to MeshCombineStudio GameObject and click \"Combine\"
    button\n2). Select in Scene debug \"Overdraw\" mode\n3). Click \"Orignal Renders
    and LodGroups\" button to swap \n\tbetween original meshes and MCS optimized
    ones.\n4). Click play and enable/disable MCS with the tab key.\n\nThe frame rate
    in Unity is capped, to see the real difference test it in a build.\nIn a build
    the FPS gain with MCS is much higher.\n\nYou can use the console to change MCS
    parameters in a build to test which\nsettings (cell size, max bounds factor,
    vertex input limit) give the best \nperformance in your case."
